		{
			"id": "eNZc8zqoPOSFOrJLY",
			"description": "Guardian Mesh Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47): blunt-trauma rules apply — any attack that fails to penetrate this DR still delivers (damage/10, rounded down, minimum 1) crushing injury to the wearer, per the flexible-armour rule for mesh, cloth and similarly soft-plate protection.\n\nLore: Worn by the Guardian militia every craftworld calls up when threatened: a fine mesh of psychoplastic and wraithbone fibres woven into a bodysuit, described throughout Codex: Craftworlds and Path of the Eldar as far lighter and less restrictive than Imperial armour of similar protection, letting a Guardian move and fight as freely as if unarmoured. framework.md's own Aeldari anchor fixes it directly: \"Flexible, DR 36 (the mesh anchor), Weak Points 5.\"\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed anchor figure: DR 36, matching (and directly justified by cross-reference to) the Imperium's own Mesh Armour entry in armour.yaml — the framework explicitly calls this \"the mesh anchor,\" so Guardian mesh is built to be mechanically identical in what it stops, honestly reflecting that mesh-class protection is mesh-class protection regardless of which culture wove it, while everything else about the entry (weight, cost, coverage, flexible-armour note) is derived independently for an Aeldari garment rather than copied wholesale. Checked with the exact dice distribution: it stops a lasgun or lasblaster hit (7d(2) burn) 9.4% of the time (90.6% get through) and a shuriken catapult hit (5d(3) cut, its own kin weapon) 9.8% of the time (90.2% get through) — genuinely thin protection against dedicated small arms, matching a Guardian militia's own status as citizen part-timers rather than dedicated soldiers, while still meaningfully better than nothing against an autogun's stub rounds (99.7% stopped) or a stray blade. Handling: 6 lb, far lighter than the Imperium's own Mesh Armour (which the Imperium entry lists heavier, being metal-reinforced) since this is a woven fibre suit rather than a plated garment, matching \"far lighter and less restrictive\" from the lore directly; full limb coverage (unlike the Imperium Flak Vest's torso-only coverage) reflects a full bodysuit rather than a vest. Weak Points 5, matching the framework's own anchor figure exactly and equal to the Imperium's Guard-pattern carapace (5). Limbs sit seven DR under the torso (29, as on the Imperium mesh), the eye lens is 20 (as on carapace visors), and the hands and feet are left at 0 (fibre gloves and slippers, not armour).",
