		{
			"id": "es2ogCSIcmag3ekgJ",
			"description": "Aspect Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47) despite the high DR: it is built from layered thermoplas plates over a flexible weave rather than rigid ceramite, so the blunt-trauma rule applies exactly as for Guardian mesh above — any attack that fails to penetrate still delivers (damage/10, rounded down, minimum 1) crushing injury.\n\nLore: The war-plate every Aspect Warrior dons on entering their shrine, distinct in look and construction between shrines (a Dire Avenger's sleek plate differs visibly from a Striking Scorpion's) but consistent in what it does: Codex: Craftworlds background and Path of the Eldar both frame Aspect armour as protection on par with a rigid suit despite being far lighter and more flexible than anything Imperial, letting an Aspect Warrior fight with an Astartes-like intensity without an Astartes's bulk. framework.md's own Aeldari anchor fixes it directly: \"Flexible thermoplas plates, DR 70, Weak Points 4.\"\n\nDesign: Held exactly at the project's fixed anchor: DR 70, deliberately equal to the Imperium carapace anchor rather than lower, because the framework is explicit this is genuinely rigid-plate-equivalent protection despite being built and worn completely differently — the flexible-armour note above is what actually distinguishes it mechanically from Imperium carapace, not a lower DR figure. Checked with the exact dice distribution: it stops a lasgun or lasblaster hit 99.4% of the time (0.6% get through, identical to the Imperium carapace-vs-lasgun figure since both sit at DR 70) and a bolter round (6dx2(2) pi++) 20.6% of the time (79.4% get through) — an Aspect Warrior in full war-plate is genuinely hard to put down with small arms, but a boltgun still kills them about as readily as it kills a Guardsman in carapace. Limbs are a few DR under the torso (64) as the framework asks, with gauntlets and greaves at 36 and the helmet eye lens at 25, well under the helmet's own DR as with every lens in this project. Handling: 14 lb, well under any Imperium rigid plate of comparable protection (carapace itself typically runs 20-25 lb in this project's own armour.yaml) for the same lighter Aeldari construction principle used throughout this file. Weak Points 4, one point tighter than Imperium Guard-pattern carapace's WP 5 and matching the Tempestus/Arbites-grade WP 4 instead — an Aspect Warrior's plate is master-crafted to their own body, with fewer gaps than mass-produced Guard carapace, but it's still articulated, flexible plate and not the near-seamless WP 3 of a Terminator's sealed suit.",
