		{
			"id": "eFSdSA5ong-DKgrrf",
			"description": "Heavy Aspect Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47), the same blunt-trauma rule as standard Aspect Armour above.\n\nLore: A bulkier, more heavily plated version of Aspect armour worn by Dark Reaper and Fire Dragon shrines, whose members carry the heaviest personal weapons (the Reaper Launcher and Fusion Gun) and, per Codex: Craftworlds background, correspondingly need — and are issued — sturdier protection than the lighter, faster shrines like the Dire Avengers or Striking Scorpions.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this variant directly, so it is interpolated between the two anchors that do exist for Aeldari plate: roughly halfway between the standard Aspect Armour anchor (DR 70) and the Exarch Armour anchor (DR 85), landing on DR 78 — extra plating for a shrine that stands and fires heavy weapons rather than closing at speed, but not the unique, individually-fitted wraithbone-fused suit an Exarch alone wears. Checked with the exact dice distribution: it stops a bolter round 36.3% of the time (up from standard Aspect Armour's 20.6%) and a shuriken catapult hit — its own kin weapon family — 99.3% of the time (up from 94.1%), a real, quantifiable step up in protection for a heavier-shrine warrior, not a cosmetic difference in name only. Limbs 72, gauntlets and greaves 40, eye lens 25. Handling: 20 lb, six pounds over the standard Aspect Armour for the extra plating, and Weak Points 4 unchanged (this is still articulated Aeldari plate with an Aspect Warrior's own fit and finish, not a rigid Exarch-grade suit — the extra weight buys DR, not fewer gaps).",
