		{
			"id": "e5RmEmUbpWX1GDZUP",
			"description": "Exarch Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47), the same blunt-trauma rule as the other Aeldari plate in this file.\n\nLore: The unique suit an Exarch is fused into on taking up their shrine's relic weapon and losing themselves to the Path of the Warrior forever; Codex: Craftworlds background is explicit that Exarch armour is wraithbone-bonded to its wearer in a way standard Aspect armour is not, part of what makes reverting to another Path effectively impossible for an Exarch. framework.md's own Aeldari anchor fixes the DR directly: \"DR 85, Weak Points 4.\"\n\nDesign: Held exactly at the project's fixed anchor: DR 85, one step above standard Aspect Armour and equal to the Imperium's own Sororitas power armour anchor — deliberately so, since both sit above ordinary rigid plate as an elite step up without reaching full Astartes-grade protection. Checked with the exact dice distribution: it stops a bolter round 54.6% of the time (up from standard Aspect Armour's 20.6%), a real, meaningful step up matching an Exarch's status as an Aspect shrine's single deadliest and most experienced warrior, while still short of true immunity to boltguns the way full Astartes plate (DR 100) approaches. Limbs 78, gauntlets and greaves 42, eye lens 30 (matching Sororitas plate). Handling: 16 lb, between the standard Aspect Armour's 14 lb and the Heavy Aspect variant's 20 lb — a wraithbone-fused suit that is denser and tougher than ordinary Aspect plate without being bulked out with extra layers the way the heavy-shrine variant is. Weak Points 4, unchanged from standard Aspect armour: an Exarch's suit is fused and unique, but it's still articulated plate built to the same joints and seams as any other Aspect armour, not a sealed Terminator-class shell.",
