		{
			"id": "eVt0Tg8Y4utYEFQzq",
			"description": "Rune Armour",
			"local_notes": "A light protective shell (DR 40, flexible per B47) plus a psychic ward that works as a regenerating shield exactly per framework.md's \"Personal force fields\" rules: Shield 60 SP, recharge after 3 seconds without taking damage at 10 SP/second, covering all attacks (as a Rosarius). Scaling: the pool given here is the baseline for a Warlock-grade wearer (Warp Empowerment 1-2); add 5 SP per level of Warp Empowerment above that baseline, to a maximum of 160 SP (a Warlock at Empowerment 6 carries 80 SP, a Farseer at 21 carries 155, in Iron Halo-to-Storm Shield territory; the rate was 20 SP per level before Empowerment was rescaled for lore-scale attack powers) — the build tool's Uses counter cannot itself scale with a trait level, so the GM sets the actual pool from the wearer's own Warp Empowerment and tracks it with Uses exactly as for any other field in fields.yaml.\n\nLore: Worn by Farseers, Warlocks and Spiritseers rather than Aspect Warriors: a suit of light robes reinforced with rune-inscribed plates that wards its wearer with their own psychic strength rather than a fixed mechanism, so a more powerful psyker's rune armour holds against far more punishment than a novice Warlock's. Codex: Craftworlds background and Path of the Eldar both describe Farseers shrugging off blows and shots that should have killed them outright, consistent with a shield that scales with the wearer rather than a flat suit of plate. framework.md's own Aeldari anchor fixes the mechanism directly: \"Psychic ward: regenerating shield (see Personal force fields), pool scaling with the wearer's Warp Empowerment.\"\n\nDesign: Built on the exact regenerating-shield chassis in fields.yaml rather than as flat DR, per the anchor's own instruction, with the DR line kept small (40, only just above Guardian mesh's 36) to represent the underlying robe rather than the ward itself — the ward, not the cloth, is what actually keeps a Farseer alive. The baseline pool (60 SP, 3-second delay, 10 SP/second recharge, all-attacks coverage) is set equal to the Imperium Rosarius, the field this project already builds for a similarly mid-tier, faith/discipline-warded wearer rather than a dedicated soldier's field, as the honest baseline for a newly-invested Warlock; the explicit per-level scaling note (+5 SP per Warp Empowerment level above that, capped at 160) is how the lore's own \"more powerful psyker, tougher ward\" relationship is captured given that GCS equipment has no mechanism to read a wearer's trait level automatically — the same \"write the scaling in notes, since the build tool can't encode a variable\" approach this project already uses for the Force Sword's Psyker Talent-scaled Force Strike line. Handling: 10 lb, lighter than any of the Aspect-class armour above since this is primarily a robe with a psychic ward, not war-plate; carries no Weak Points rating, since the ward (not physical armour) is what actually turns most hits aside, matching how the Imperium's own force-field items in fields.yaml carry no Weak Points rating either.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker",
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield"
			],
