		{
			"id": "e-vrTnJx83t5CTfGn",
			"description": "Ranger Cameleoline Cloak",
			"local_notes": "The bonuses already stand for the cloak's light-bending; there is no separate penalty to observers' Vision rolls. Does not stack with a second cameleoline garment.\n\nLore: Every Ranger wraps themselves in a cameleoline cloak woven to bend light around its wearer, the signature garment of the Aeldari who walk the Path of the Outcast; Codex: Craftworlds and the Path of the Eldar background (no specific rules entry) treat it as best-in-setting personal camouflage technology, letting a Ranger vanish against almost any backdrop while moving carefully.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a large, explicit Stealth and Camouflage skill bonus rather than DR, per the assignment's own call for \"a strong Stealth/Camouflage bonus\" — a cameleoline cloak's whole purpose is not being seen, not stopping a hit once found, so it carries no `dr` field at all, the opposite design choice from every armour entry above it in this file. +2 Stealth is a solid but unexceptional gear bonus, and +4 Camouflage reflects that Camouflage itself (the skill used to actually set up concealment before combat, not just move stealthily during it) is the cloak's real specialty. Two bonuses and no separate Vision penalty keeps it strong without out-stacking the Imperium's camo cloaks. Handling: 3 lb, a garment rather than armour — it carries no ST requirement, Weak Points rating or coverage, since it protects by not being found rather than by stopping a hit.",
